WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.616
Stormwater inspections are kept on the Reports page.

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:08.900
Here is the running list, newest on top, each one marked draft or completed.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:14.720
Start today's. The header already knows who you are, your credential and the permit.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.579
Everything else carries forward from last time.

00:00:18.293 --> 00:00:22.013
The disturbed area summary refreshes from the tracker log.

00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:24.963
One tap, and the acres are the acres you drew.

00:00:25.664 --> 00:00:30.677
Drainage areas and discharge points carry forward from the last inspection.

00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:35.624
Mark them acceptable in one tap. Flip one to deficient and the note opens.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:39.025
Every practice from the SWPPP is a row.

00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:42.689
Installed, condition, maintenance, corrective action.

00:00:43.394 --> 00:00:46.667
Corrective actions collect themselves from what you flagged.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.194
Add your own if you need to.

00:00:48.895 --> 00:00:53.645
Photos you tagged for stormwater since the last inspection are already here.

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:57.554
Sign it on the screen, with a finger or a stylus.

00:00:57.554 --> 00:01:03.291
Complete locks the record, and offers to carry what you flagged into the compliance log.

00:01:03.291 --> 00:01:07.659
Reopening asks you to confirm, because this is a regulatory record.

00:01:08.363 --> 00:01:14.553
Export a PDF or a Word file in the format the agency expects, and send it from your phone.
